From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use the updated horizontal logos

The package shows its own versions of the two horizontal logos, the
banner in README.md and the site header's wide variant, which were
updated by hand on main. Vendoring copies upstream's logo/ into
man/figures/ on every run, so this patch turns the copied horizontal
logos, DuckDB_Logo-horizontal.svg and DuckDB_Logo-horizontal-dark-mode.svg,
into the package's. The stacked pair, logo.svg and logo-dark-mode.svg,
equals upstream's and needs no patch.

It retires itself once upstream ships these logos: the run then finds
the change already in the regenerated tree and removes the patch.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/man/figures/DuckDB_Logo-horizontal.svg b/man/figures/DuckDB_Logo-horizontal.svg
--- a/man/figures/DuckDB_Logo-horizontal.svg
+++ b/man/figures/DuckDB_Logo-horizontal.svg
